[182.557959, "o", "Setup complete. All artifacts are in place:\r\n\r\n- **Base model + tokenizer (configured for 20 classes):** `/app/model_cache/xlm-roberta-base`\r\n- **LoRA adapter merged into the base model:** `/app/merged_model/`\r\n- **Detection results:** `/app/detection_results.json`\r\n\r\nThe adapter's classifier head loaded correctly (20 output classes), and the merged model was verified on the 10 test samples. Predictions were:\r\n\r\n| Text | Predicted class ID | Confidence |\r\n|---|---:|---:|\r\n| Bonjour, comment allez-vous aujourd'hui? | 6 | 0.9753 |\r\n| Hola, ¿cómo estás hoy? | 5 | 0.9890 |\r\n| Guten Tag, wie geht es Ihnen? | 2 | 0.9973 |\r\n| Ciao, come stai oggi? | 8 | 0.9888 |\r\n| Olá, como você está? | 12 | 0.9896 |\r\n| Привет, как дела? | 13 | 0.9856 |\r\n| こんにちは、お元気ですか？ | 9 | 0.9649 |\r\n| 你好，你好吗？ | 19 | 0.9360 |\r\n| مرحبا، كيف حالك؟ | 0 | 0.9880 |\r\n| Hello, how are you? | 4 | 0.9737 |\r\n\r\nI also spot-checked one sample from each of the remaining 10 adapter langua"]
[182.558139, "o", "ges (Bulgarian, Greek, Hindi, Dutch, Polish, Swahili, Thai, Turkish, Urdu, Vietnamese); all resolved to distinct expected class IDs with 0.98–0.997 confidence.\r\n\r\n`detection_results.json` follows the requested schema with `text`, `predicted_class_id`, and `confidence`.\r\n"]
